<section class="business-section" id="signals">
  <div class="business-wrap">
    <div class="business-section-head">
      <div>
        <span class="business-eyebrow">How I help</span>
        <h2>It usually comes down to three questions.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="business-section-intro">What to build, how to build it, and who builds it with you. I've had to answer all three with my own money and time on the line.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="business-signals">
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">What should we actually build?</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Founders rarely need more features — they need a direction they can commit to. I've run product discovery on my own startups, including more than 1,000 customer conversations at Butler AI and several hard pivots, so I know how expensive the wrong direction gets.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">Which technical calls are hard to undo?</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Architecture, build-versus-buy, what ships first. I've owned systems that scaled to tens of millions of events a second and broken monoliths into services without downtime. I make these calls with founders instead of leaving them to luck.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">How do you turn a few engineers into a team that ships?</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Hiring, ownership, and how people actually work together. I've led teams of up to eight engineers, built interview processes from scratch, and cared as much about the culture as the code.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
